<title>UK: Bass advances on Goldman upgrade.</title>
<headline>Bass advances on Goldman upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Bass Plc advanced to their highest level in four four and a half months as Goldman Sachs added the stock to its European priority list, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0903 GMT, the shares were up 13p to 834-1/2p.  </p>
<p>The brokerage previously had recommended Bass shares as a &quot;buy&quot; and had not increased earnings estimates, dealers said.</p>
<p>The upgrade, they added, was based on expectations of a rotation into consumer stocks.</p>
<p>Goldman analysts could not be immediately reached for comment.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
